# Test: the theme and the sidebar width persist across a reload
# VALIDATES: spec-fleet-ui-1 user story 6, AC-4's preferences and A-2 --
#            the theme switch writes the browser setting ze-theme, which
#            fleet-theme.js applies to the root element before the first
#            paint of the next load; the sidebar handle writes its width,
#            which fleet.js sets as the custom property --fleet-sidebar-width
#            on the root element through the object model
# PREVENTS: a theme or a width that holds for one page and is lost on the
#           next load, and a width script that silently takes the three-class
#           fallback because the browser refused the custom property
#
# Goal: prove the two shell preferences survive a reload in a browser.
# Method: the root element carries no data-theme until a choice is stored
# (shell.templ Shell), and the switch flips it light, then dark
# (fleet.js toggleTheme). The test switches twice, reloading after each, and
# reads data-theme on the root with the attribute expectation, so a reload
# that drew the server's default would fail on the first value and a stored
# choice that never changes would fail on the second. The width is set from
# the keyboard on the handle, End being the maximum of 28rem (fleet.js
# SIDEBAR_MAX), because the format has no drag; the test reads the handle's
# aria-valuenow, which both paths of applyWidth set, and the root's style,
# which only the custom property path writes. That second read is what
# validates A-2: under the fallback the root's style stays empty.
# What remains a human check is the drag itself (pointer events on the
# handle), which no .wb action can perform.

option=needs-build-tag:value=ze_fleet_ui_sample:state=present
option=timeout:value=90s
option=viewport:width=1600:height=1000

action=open:path=/fleet/
expect=element:id=fleet-sidebar-handle

# The theme: light, kept by a reload, then dark, kept by a reload.
action=click:text=Account menu
action=click:text=Switch theme
expect=attribute:selector=html:name=data-theme:value=light
action=open:path=/fleet/
expect=element:id=fleet-sidebar-handle
expect=attribute:selector=html:name=data-theme:value=light
action=click:text=Account menu
action=click:text=Switch theme
expect=attribute:selector=html:name=data-theme:value=dark
action=open:path=/fleet/
expect=element:id=fleet-sidebar-handle
expect=attribute:selector=html:name=data-theme:value=dark

# The width: the maximum, from the keyboard, kept by a reload.
expect=attribute:selector=#fleet-sidebar-handle:name=aria-valuenow:value=17
action=press:id=fleet-sidebar-handle:key=End
expect=attribute:selector=#fleet-sidebar-handle:name=aria-valuenow:value=28
expect=attribute:selector=html:name=style:contains=--fleet-sidebar-width: 28rem
action=open:path=/fleet/
expect=element:id=fleet-sidebar-handle
expect=attribute:selector=#fleet-sidebar-handle:name=aria-valuenow:value=28
expect=attribute:selector=html:name=style:contains=--fleet-sidebar-width: 28rem
